Subject: [LOCAL RESEARCH] vmapple: cache protected CTRR RAM through one shared ROMD backing

Local experiment, not intended for upstream submission. Borrow the existing
RAMBlock identity for a full-sized ROMD view and map validated read-only
ranges through aliases. Normal CPU/DMA writes still return MEMTX_ERROR;
enabled writable ranges use ordinary RAM/SMC handling. No RAM copy, second
RAMBlock, PAuth change, or new migration support. Reset/unrealize remove
range mappings; the borrowed reference lives until the view owner finalizes.
Privileged debugger/ROM-loading access keeps standard QEMU ROMD semantics.

